  <title>The README of a project</title>
  <p>Each project has a README, the file <file>README.md</file> of its folder: what the lab is for, its addresses, how to use it. The <gui>Readme</gui> tab shows it rendered. The Projects window shows it too, and the Import window its first paragraph.</p>
  <figure>
    <title>The Readme tab</title>
    <media type="image" mime="image/png" src="figures/readme.png">
      <p>The Readme tab: the README rendered, with a heading, a paragraph, a list and a link; Edit and Preview over the top right corner.</p>
    </media>
  </figure>
  <p>Two buttons float over the top right corner of the tab: <gui>Edit</gui> opens the text, and <gui>Preview</gui> goes back to the rendered README. While you write, <gui>Syntax</gui> shows what the text can hold. The README is saved 30 seconds after your last change, and when you leave the tab.</p>
  <terms>
    <title>The syntax</title>
    <item>
      <title><code># Title</code></title>
      <p>A heading; <code>##</code> for a smaller one.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><code>*emphasis*</code>, <code>**strong**</code>, <code>~~struck~~</code></title>
      <p>Emphasis, strong and struck text.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><code>`code`</code></title>
      <p>Code; <code>```</code> above and below a block of it.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><code>- item</code></title>
      <p>A list; <code>1.</code> for a numbered one.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><code>&gt; quote</code></title>
      <p>A quote.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><code>[text](https://example.org)</code></title>
      <p>A link, which opens in your browser; a bare URL is one too.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><code>![The lab](topology.png)</code></title>
      <p>A picture: a file of the folder of the project, of at most 10 MB.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><code>---</code></title>
      <p>A line across.</p>
    </item>
  </terms>
  <p>Anything else shows as you typed it. A new line in a paragraph stays a new line, so a README written as plain text keeps its lines.</p>
</page>
